---
source: tests/cli/help_snapshots_test.rs
expression: "help_output(&[subcommand, \"--help\"])"
---
Add a topic subtree from YAML, JSON, or Markdown input.

Usage: xmind add-tree [OPTIONS] --parent <PARENT> <--dry-run|--apply> <WORKBOOK>

Arguments:
  <WORKBOOK>  Path to the .xmind workbook

Options:
      --parent <PARENT>                Parent topic selector
      --input <INPUT>                  YAML or JSON tree input file
      --from-markdown <FROM_MARKDOWN>  Markdown outline input file
      --markdown-mode <MARKDOWN_MODE>  Markdown outline parsing mode [possible values: heading, list, hybrid, auto]
      --dry-run                        Preview the change without writing the workbook
      --apply                          Write the change to the workbook
      --backup                         Create a safety backup before applying changes
      --json                           Emit a JSON command envelope
      --format <FORMAT>                Select the human or machine-readable output format [default: text] [possible values: text, json, compact-json, markdown, outline, assets]
      --fields <FIELDS>                Limit JSON output to comma-separated field paths
      --quiet                          Suppress non-essential text output
      --no-color                       Disable ANSI color in text output
      --sheet <SHEET>                  Select a sheet by title
      --sheet-id <SHEET_ID>            Select a sheet by stable id
      --sheet-index <SHEET_INDEX>      Select a sheet by zero-based index
  -h, --help                           Print help

Examples:
  xmind add-tree roadmap.xmind --parent path:/Launch --input tree.yaml --dry-run
  xmind add-tree roadmap.xmind --parent path:/Launch --from-markdown notes.md --markdown-mode auto --dry-run
